{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that repairs Java 11 code so that it correctly solves the given programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Repair the following Java 11 code so that it correctly solves the programming problem. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your repaired code should implement the problem correctly, meaning that it should produce the correct output for any valid input.\nPrint your repaired code and also the confidence score you give to your repair. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<repaired_code>\n<your_repaired_code>\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the problem description:\n<problem_description>\nMr. Chanek has an integer represented by a string $$$s$$$. Zero or more digits have been erased and are denoted by the character _. There are also zero or more digits marked by the character X, meaning they're the same digit.Mr. Chanek wants to count the number of possible integer $$$s$$$, where $$$s$$$ is divisible by $$$25$$$. Of course, $$$s$$$ must not contain any leading zero. He can replace the character _ with any digit. He can also replace the character X with any digit, but it must be the same for every character X.As a note, a leading zero is any 0 digit that comes before the first nonzero digit in a number string in positional notation. For example, 0025 has two leading zeroes. An exception is the integer zero, (0 has no leading zero, but 0000 has three leading zeroes).\n</problem_description>\n\nHere is the Java 11 code you have to repair:\n<original_code>\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    private static char[] arr;\n    private static final String[] suffixes = {\"00\", \"25\", \"50\", \"75\"};\n    private static long ans = 0;\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        BufferedReader br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        arr = br.readLine().toCharArray();\n        ans = 0;\n\n        if (arr.length >= 2) {\n            for (String suf : suffixes) {\n                handleLastTwo(arr[arr.length - 2], arr[arr.length - 1], suf);\n            }\n        } else {\n            if (arr[0] == '0' || arr[0] == 'X' || arr[0] == '_') {\n                ans++;\n            }\n        }\n\n        System.out.println(ans);\n        br.close();\n    }\n\n    private static void handleLastTwo(char c1, char c2, String suf) {\n        char a = c1;\n        char b = c2;\n\n        if (a == '_' && suf.charAt(0) == '0' && arr.length - 2 == 0) return;\n\n        if (a == 'X') {\n            a = suf.charAt(0);\n            if (b == 'X') b = suf.charAt(0);\n        }\n        if (b == 'X') {\n            b = suf.charAt(1);\n            if (a == 'X') a = suf.charAt(1);\n        }\n        if (a == '_') a = suf.charAt(0);\n        if (b == '_') b = suf.charAt(1);\n\n        char xChar = 'n';\n        if (c1 == 'X') xChar = a;\n        if (c2 == 'X') xChar = b;\n\n        if (a == suf.charAt(0) && b == suf.charAt(1)) {\n            computeCount(xChar);\n        }\n    }\n\n    private static void computeCount(char x) {\n        if ((x == '0' && arr[0] == 'X') || arr[0] == '0') return;\n\n        long ways = 1;\n        boolean hasX = x != 'n';\n\n        for (int i = 0; i < arr.length - 2; i++) {\n            if (arr[i] == '_') {\n                ways *= (i == 0) ? 9 : 10;\n            }\n            if (!hasX && arr[i] == 'X') {\n                hasX = true;\n                ways *= (i == 0) ? 9 : 10;\n            }\n        }\n\n        ans += ways;\n    }\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<repaired_code>\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    private static char[] arr;\n    private static final String[] suffixes = {\"00\", \"25\", \"50\", \"75\"};\n    private static long ans = 0;\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        BufferedReader br = new BufferedReader(new InputStreamReader(System.in));\n        arr = br.readLine().toCharArray();\n        ans = 0;\n\n        if (arr.length >= 2) {\n            for (String suf : suffixes) {\n                handleLastTwo(suf);\n            }\n        } else {\n            if (arr[0] == '0' || arr[0] == 'X' || arr[0] == '_') {\n                ans++;\n            }\n        }\n\n        System.out.println(ans);\n        br.close();\n    }\n\n    private static void handleLastTwo(String suf) {\n        char a = arr[arr.length - 2];\n        char b = arr[arr.length - 1];\n\n        // Check if the last two characters can match the suffix\n        if (!canMatch(a, suf.charAt(0)) || !canMatch(b, suf.charAt(1))) {\n            return;\n        }\n\n        // Check for leading zero constraint\n        if (arr.length >= 3 && suf.charAt(0) == '0' && arr[arr.length - 2] == '_') {\n            // If the second-to-last position is '_' and we're trying to put '0' there,\n            // and it's the first digit (position 0), then it would be a leading zero\n            if (arr.length - 2 == 0) {\n                return;\n            }\n        }\n        \n        // Check if the first digit would be '0' when it's a single digit or the first position\n        if (arr.length == 1) {\n            if (suf.charAt(0) == '0' && arr[0] == '_') {\n                ans++;\n                return;\n            }\n        }\n\n        // Determine if there are X characters and what digit they represent\n        char xChar = 'n';\n        boolean hasX = false;\n        \n        if (arr[arr.length - 2] == 'X' || arr[arr.length - 1] == 'X') {\n            hasX = true;\n            xChar = suf.charAt(0); // Both X's must be the same digit\n        }\n\n        // Check for conflicts with X characters\n        if (arr[arr.length - 2] == 'X' && arr[arr.length - 1] == 'X') {\n            if (suf.charAt(0) != suf.charAt(1)) {\n                return; // X's must be same digit, but suffix has different digits\n            }\n        } else if (arr[arr.length - 2] == 'X') {\n            if (suf.charAt(0) != suf.charAt(1)) {\n                return;\n            }\n        } else if (arr[arr.length - 1] == 'X') {\n            if (suf.charAt(0) != suf.charAt(1)) {\n                return;\n            }\n        }\n\n        // Count valid combinations for the remaining digits\n        long ways = 1;\n        \n        for (int i = 0; i < arr.length - 2; i++) {\n            if (arr[i] == '_') {\n                ways *= (i == 0) ? 9 : 10;\n            } else if (arr[i] == 'X') {\n                if (i == 0) {\n                    ways *= 9;\n                } else {\n                    ways *= 10;\n                }\n            }\n        }\n\n        ans += ways;\n    }\n\n    private static boolean canMatch(char actual, char expected) {\n        if (actual == '_') return true;\n        if (actual == 'X') return true;\n        return actual == expected;\n    }\n}\n</repaired_code>\n<confidence>\n0.5\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-2.3841855067985307e-07, -6.496695277746767e-05, -4.6491513785440475e-06, 0.0, -1.0251946150674485e-05, -3.361645576660521e-05, -3.576278118089249e-07, -9.65590606938349e-06, -2.9444261599564925e-05, -1.7404405298293568e-05, -2.3841855067985307e-07, -8.475421054754406e-05, -1.5497195136049413e-06, -1.0728830375228426e-06, -3.3378546504536644e-06, -1.0132738680113107e-05, -8.344646857949556e-07, -0.00021872512297704816, -1.6689286894688848e-06, -0.048646945506334305, -1.1920922133867862e-06, -0.0011993603548035026, -0.0005094899097457528, -2.622600959512056e-06, -2.9802276912960224e-06, -2.0146166207268834e-05, -0.0016471878625452518, -0.00019012074335478246, -3.